findings.body:
The `Promise.all` in `initServices()` now calls `scheduling.init()` with no arguments. `post-scheduling/index.js` evaluates `options.apiUrl` after an `await`, so `options` is `undefined` and the async `init` rejects with a TypeError. `Promise.all` rejects, and `initServices()` fails. Ghost cannot start.

The original call passed `apiUrl: urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)`. The PR removed that argument, but `urlUtils` is still required on line 343. The argument is needed. The PR description says nothing about this change, and it has nothing to do with removing xmlrpc.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="366-369"}

::callout{type="security"}
This is a boot-time failure, not a degraded feature. Restore the original `apiUrl` option so the scheduler receives the Admin API URL.

::suggestion{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="368-370"}
scheduling.init({
    apiUrl: urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)
}),

The `Promise.all` no longer calls `slack.listen()`. In `server/services/slack.js`, `listen()` is what subscribes `slackListener` to `post.published` and `slackTestPing` to `slack.test`. Without it, Slack webhook notifications for published posts stop, and the Slack "test" button in admin does nothing. No error is logged, so this regression would not be caught in production.

The `slack` require on line 319 is now unused, which is the leftover you would expect from an accidental deletion. The PR description only mentions xmlrpc, so this removal does not look intentional.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="351-362"}

::callout{type="warning"}
If Slack is meant to be removed too, the PR needs to say so and delete `slack.js`, its test, and the `slack_*` settings handling. If not, restore `slack.listen(),` in the `Promise.all`.

`emailAddressService.init()` used to be awaited before the `Promise.all`. It now runs inside the array. `EmailAddressServiceWrapper.init()` is synchronous, and array elements are evaluated in order, so `emailService` still sees an initialised address service. The ordering is correct today, but it now depends on the array order rather than on an explicit `await`.

The NOTE comment above it ("newsletter service and email service depend on email address service") now sits above an empty line, with no code under it. Move the comment next to the `emailAddressService.init()` entry, or restore the sequential `await`.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="349-352"}

The PR deletes `xmlrpc.test.js` and adds no replacement. The remaining unit tests cover each service's `listen()` or `init()` in isolation. Nothing exercises `initServices()`, so a call that throws at boot, or a dropped listener, passes CI. The removed xmlrpc tests did not cover this path either.

A small test that boots `initServices()` with the real service modules, or at least checks that `scheduling.init` receives an `apiUrl`, and that `slack.listen` is still invoked, would have caught both regressions above.

::code{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="351-368"}
